<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sultan Hasanuddin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1631">1631</a>–<a href="/years/1670">1670</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Hasanuddin of Gowa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Hasanuddin was the sixteenth ruler of the Makassarese kingdom of Gowa in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>, reigning from 1653 to 1669. He resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>'s attempts to monopolise the spice trade, but was defeated by a VOC force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornelis-speelman">Cornelis Speelman</a> allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arung-palakka">Arung Palakka</a> and had to accept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-bongaya">Treaty of Bongaya</a> in 1667. He is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-hero-of-indonesia">National Hero of Indonesia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sultan-hasanuddin.jpg" alt="Sultan Hasanuddin" width="320" height="570" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Torbenbrinker · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MonumentSultanHasanuddin.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
